# Per-run screenshot outputs; only the *-reference.png baselines are tracked.
*-current.png
*-diff.png

# Bloom-regenerated files fall in two classes.
#
# 1. Rendering-relevant CSS (branding.css, appearance.css, defaultLangStyles.css,
#    origami.css, langVisibility.css) is COMMITTED, deliberately: when a reference
#    screenshot breaks, the diff of these snapshots can name the cause. Tests never
#    write into this repo (they run Bloom on a temp copy), so the snapshots only move
#    when someone refreshes them on purpose — refresh them whenever you update the
#    reference screenshots. Default branding only.
#
# 1b. basePage.css and previewMode.css stay ignored even though Bloom copies them in
#    and they affect rendering: they are byte copies of stylesheets versioned in the
#    BloomDesktop repo, so their forensic record already exists there, tied to this
#    repo through build/testing-inputs.pin. Committing them here would only churn on
#    every Bloom version.
collections/**/basePage.css
collections/**/previewMode.css
#
# 2. Run artifacts stay ignored: the suite switches brandings mid-run, so these hold
#    whichever branding ran last, and history.db is a binary that changes on every
#    open. Their diffs carry noise, not evidence.
collections/**/thumbnail.png
collections/**/coverImage*.jpg
collections/**/license.png
collections/**/made-with-bloom-badge*.svg
collections/**/lang-qr-code.png
collections/**/history.db
# Branding xmatter stylesheets and logos copied in for whichever branding is active.
collections/**/*-XMatter.css
collections/**/USAID_*
collections/**/Uzbekistan-*
collections/**/UEEP\[*\]*.svg
collections/**/BloomLocal.svg
collections/**/BloomWithTaglineAgainstLight.svg
collections/**/Bloom Against Light HD.png

node_modules
*.log
.DS_Store
